Done — 61 commits on `main`, all pushed, clean working tree.

**Games now have a memory.** Each of the six rounds writes a record through a new [gameResults.js](src/utils/gameResults.js) (best score, the scale it was won on, and how many rounds finished). The hub reads it: each card gains a `Best 1200 of 1600 · 3 rounds played` line ([Games.js](src/screens/Games.js)), and a "Last played" strip above the grid offers the game you were just in. The scales are kept per game because Concept Scrabble pays 500 a term and Concept Check pays 10 a question — a bare number would invite a comparison between rounds that measure different things. Knowledge Chain was the last holdout: it now records only when the eighth chain is solved, since a chain is a question and the set is the round.

**The dictionary stopped being a lookup table.** Entries can be ordered A→Z, Z→A, by subject, or shortest-first ([Dictionary.js](src/screens/Dictionary.js)); `/` jumps to the search box; the characters you typed are marked inside each term and tagline via [HighlightedText.js](src/components/HighlightedText.js); an open entry ends with a row of related entries and a "Copy link" button. `#/term/{id}` now actually opens the entry it names — the hash parser already read the id and the app used to drop it.

Related entries are derived, not authored, in [relations.ts](src/data/dictionary/relations.ts): shared distinctive words, weighted towards the term itself, with one shared word in the prose explicitly *not* counting (an early draft paired Cognitive Dissonance with the Banality of Evil on the strength of "individuals"). The row is labelled Related, not prerequisite, because it is a heuristic.

**Verification:** `938 tests / 91 suites` pass, `tsc --noEmit` clean, `npm run lint` and `lint:all` both clean. The last two commits fixed pre-existing lint errors rather than suppressing them — tests were reading `.definition-text` and `.quiz-review` out of the DOM by class name, so the components grew `data-testid`s.
