{"kind":"tool","id":"h-uT-ezzBmk","toolName":"write_file","input":{"path":"src/styles/print.css","instructions":"Add a print stylesheet for lessons and legal documents.","content":"/* ==========================================================================
   print.css — the paper edition
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Velora is a reference book, and a reference book is allowed to leave the
   browser. Printing the app as it stands produces something close to a
   screenshot: the dock prints, the theme switch prints, the toast prints if it
   happens to be open, and the dark theme prints as a solid black page.

   This file is loaded last and only applies inside @media print. It does three
   things and nothing else:

   1. Forces the daylight edition. Paper is white and ink is black, whatever the
      reader had chosen on screen.
   2. Removes every element that only exists to be pressed.
   3. Sets the text as a document — serif, 11pt, a 68-character measure, and a
      page break before each lesson section so a long read is not split through
      the middle of a paragraph.

   It deliberately does not restyle individual screens. A screen that prints
   badly is a screen whose reading column is wrong, and that is fixed in the
   screen's own stylesheet.
   ========================================================================== */

@media print {
  :root,
  :root[data-theme='dark'] {
    --bg-primary: #FFFFFF;
    --bg-secondary: #FFFFFF;
    --bg-tertiary: #F4F0E8;
